#N canvas 20 20 1000 860 12;
#X text 20 20 e_tail -- when a reverb engine runs \, in each of e_verb's three: on as soon as it is wanted \, and once it is not \, off when its tail has died \, below -80 dBFS for 300 ms. So an engine left by a change of type \, or by the last send going to 0 \, rings out and then stops costing anything (Brendan \, 2026-11-05). ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 150 creation args: none. inlet 1: 1 or 0 \, whether its engine is wanted: the type chosen \, with a send above 0. inlet 2: the engine's level \, from its env~ \, in dB. outlet 1: 1 or 0 \, for the engine's switch~. outlet 2: a bang just before the 0 \, to clear the engine's delay lines., f 70;
#X obj 20 260 inlet;
#X obj 500 260 inlet;
#X obj 20 300 t f f f;
#X obj 300 420 f;
#X obj 160 340 sel 1;
#X msg 160 380 1;
#X obj 500 300 < 20;
#X obj 500 340 change;
#X obj 500 380 t b f;
#X obj 20 460 expr \$f1 == 0 && \$f2;
#X obj 20 500 change;
#X obj 20 540 sel 1 0;
#X msg 120 580 stop;
#X obj 20 620 del 300;
#X obj 20 660 t b b;
#X msg 20 700 0;
#X obj 20 760 outlet;
#X obj 300 760 outlet;
#X text 500 460 Idle is not wanted and quiet: the 300 ms start when it begins \, and stop if it ends \, so a tail still sounding when the engine stops being wanted keeps it on until the tail is below -80 dBFS. A wanted engine is on at once \, and never idle. Its env~ runs only while it is on \, so the level it last gave stands while it is off \, and a level from before is put right within one of env~'s periods \, 46 ms \, of switching on: far inside the 300., f 50;
